    <string name="settings_section_help">Help</string>
    <string name="settings_help_setup">Set things up in this order: create a “Credential” (username plus password or private key), then a “Tunnel” (frpc STCP visitor), then a “Connection” that ties the two together. Picking a tunnel derives Host/Port from it, so there is nothing to type.</string>
    <string name="settings_help_tmux">tmux: “Probe remote sessions” in the connection editor lists what is already running so you can attach to it, create a new one, or skip tmux. With tmux a dropped link resumes exactly where it left off; without it, a drop loses the shell.</string>
    <string name="settings_help_keys">Terminal key row: ESC / CTRL / arrows (hold to repeat) / TAB / S-TAB / ^C / ^D / Home / End / PgUp / PgDn and more — swipe it sideways. CTRL is sticky: tap it, then a letter, for Ctrl+letter.</string>
    <string name="settings_help_troubleshoot">When a connection fails, work down: the diagnostics above, then that tunnel\'s log on the Tunnels tab (all of frpc\'s output lands there), then whether the remote sshd and its port are reachable at all.</string>

